                        <item name="Description" type_name="gh_string" type_code="10">Who runs the admittance solves. Auto: the OpenCL GPU when one answers, else the CPU; a fallback is reported as a warning. CPU: the FFT solve per distinct orientation. GPU: the same filter as a direct convolution on the device (measured within 1e-5 K of the FFT), and refuse to run silently on the CPU. Pays off on grids with thousands of DISTINCT orientations (curved facades); a flat grid is one solve either way.</item>
