                      <items count="7">
                        <item name="Access" type_name="gh_int32" type_code="3">1</item>
                        <item name="Description" type_name="gh_string" type_code="10">What the ground of each Layer Outlines curve IS: water, sand, rock, grass, park, pitch, scrub, farmland, orchard, bare_soil, residential, industrial, forest, garden, and roads, paved, paths. Every kind lies inside one Davenport class, so Layer Roughness stays right for it. Wire it to the Layer Names input of City Surface INSTEAD of Layer Names to split and colour its layers by what the ground is rather than by roughness class (a result saved before this output holds the class names).</item>
